<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16226" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrythēa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-_ia</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρύθεια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small island in the
				Bay of Cadiz</i>, <i>where the giant Geryon
			dwelt</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 6, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 21,
				36, § 120</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 5, 9,
				2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrythīus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Erythean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad litora Gades,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					16, 195</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕrythēïs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>Erythean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 543</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 5, 649</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
